  ],
  "text": "Question nine. When do you choose threads versus multiprocessing versus async? Match the tool to the bottleneck. The deciding question is always: is the program waiting on IO, or burning CPU? Waiting, on many connections: async. One thread, the lowest overhead. Waiting, but through blocking libraries: threads, which release the gill while they wait, in a pool that caps how many run. Burning CPU: multiprocessing. Separate processes sidestep the gill for true parallelism. And real services mix them: an async server that hands its heavy computation to a process pool.",
